1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was Bonde i Djäkneboda 5, whose 2 sons die in war with Russia.
2 CONT Shown at Djäkneboda 5, Bygdeå, A1:2.8, with kids, and with wife #1, dying in 1749.
2 CONT Shown at  Djäkneboda 5, A1:3.45, in with wife #3, as retired parents (1762-1771).
2 CONT His brother Pehr lucks out by marrying a rich girl next door to become bonde at Djäkneboda 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife Karin died, leaving 3 year old Abe (our ancestor), 2 year old sister, and 5 other kids.
2 CONT A 1/2 year later stepmother Margareta Klingberg-Persdotter of Själevad enters (no record of what happened to her; perhaps failed probation?).
2 CONT Then, nine years later, girl-next-door, Lisa Wanichsdotter, arrives on the scene (stepmother Lisa's is a bit younger and a daughter in military family--comes with a pretty good pedigree).
2 CONT
2 CONT Dies 1769-04-07 at 79 years from kräfta i ryggen (cancer in the back).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Agneta Olofsson, "Bygdeå byar och gårdar 1600 - 1800 " (1999), pp. 58-59, Djäkneboda 4 continued, cites DII:1.53 (1726-53) and 1730, 1755, and 1759 Dombok entries.
2 CONT Kråken 24 database person 276827, https://kråken.se/ gives source as HFL (birth) & C:2 (death); HFL: Djäkneboda, Bygdeå AI:2.8 (1746-62) b. 1699.
2 CONT
