1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Born to Jon Andersson at Djäkneboda, Bygdeå, AI:2.8. The ancestoral farm went to his brother, so he left and married in wife's town of Rickleå, Bygdeå and lived the remainder of his life there. He becomes soldier 
2 CONC #42 in Rickleå, Bygdeå, Trumflagare (Drummer), adopting the name "Hök." Shown as soldier #48 living  with wife and family, AI:4.160 (1771-88), until in 1785 he is sent off to fight off the Russian onslaught that sacked Västerbotte
2 CONC n. He died 1790 at age 44 in the war with Russia. His brother, Anders, soldier #3 in Bygdeå, also died in 1790, at age 53, in the war with Russia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Agneta Olofsson "Bygdeå Byar och Gårdar," p. 481, Höök/Hök 42, cites AI:4.160 (1771-94).
