2 CONT
2 CONT Febris maligna = rotting fever
2 CONT
2 CONT Burden fever: an older medical collective name for a variety of epidemic febrile diseases. The common name meant that putrid fever was used as a diagnosis for many different disease processes: high fever with symptoms of bodily pu
2 CONC trefaction, such as a putrid fetid smell or foul-smelling rash, febrile diseases such as typhoid fever and spotted typhus, as well as situations where death was the result of blood poisoning, to example in case of gangrene (gangre
2 CONC ne).
