1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Innkeeper's daughter. She is shown with parents Johan Klingström A. and Fattenborg at Rickleå 13, AI:2.48 (1746-62). Then she is shown as wife of soldier #48 living  with husband and family, AI:4.160 (1771-1788). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and burial record:"[1809] Maji [died May] 1, [buried May] 7, Enkan [Widow] Anna Johans Dr. i Rikleå död  i Feber [Fever, age] 69 år gl. Testamente till Kyrkan 8 Dr [Daler] Fattige 8 Dr [Daler] Banco" [8 dalar to the church, 
2 CONC 8 daler to the poor].
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Bygdeå parish record: C2.175 (marriage).
2 CONT Death & burial record, Bygdeå (AC) C:3.653 (1781-1829), NAD SE/HLA/1010025/C/3 bildid: C0034039_00341, https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/C0034039_00341 or AID: v139128.b319.s653, https://app.arkivdigital.se/volume/v139128?ima
2 CONC ge=319
2 CONT Testament at death is also recorded at Bygdeå Räkenskaper för kyrka, LI:4.42 (1805-1822), NAD SE/HLA/1010025/L I/4 (1805-1822), bildid: C0034046_00042, https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/C0034046_00042
2 CONT Agneta Olofsson, "Bygdeå byar och gårdar 1600 - 1800" (2006), p. 424, No. 42 Höök/Hök continued.
2 CONT Kråken 13 person 193578, https://kråken.se/ gives sources "HFL,FR" (birth) and "HFL) (death); HFL: wife and widow on Miltårer AI:5b.185 (1784-90) and widow on Rickleå, Bygdeå AI:6.280 (1797-1806)
