1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was daughter of soldier #42-48 in Rickleå, Bygdeå, who died age 44 in 1790 in war with Russia. She is shown living with parents + siblings, A1:4.160 (1771-88). Brother and father are sent off to fight off Russi
2 CONC an onslaught, which sacked Västerbotten.
2 CONT In marriage book:
2 CONT Abrahamsdotter, Lisa Catharina .Soldatdotter Rickleå
2 CONT ...1792-10-22     (aka Caisa) innkeeper's granddaughter
2 CONT ...Nathanaelsson, Nils .Nybyggare (settler at) Bjänfors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note how many children of her first marriage who did not survive: son 19.5 weeks magsjuka (stomach flu), son 6 weeks oangiven sjuka (declared sick), daughter Margareta 7 weeks magsjuka, son Nils 4.5 days oangiven sjuka, daughter U
2 CONC lrica 12 weeks magsjuka, son Nils 1 year 3 mo. okän sjukdom (unknown disease); son Nils 14 days okän sjukdom, etc. No children from second marriage except one stillborn child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Shown on A1: 4.37 (1771-88) as newlywed @ inlaws+Nils in Bjänsfors 1.
2 CONT Shown on A1:5A.86 (1784+1797) in Åkullsjön farm #1 with husband + kids.
2 CONT Shown on A1:6 (1797-1807) in Åkullsjön farm #1 w/ wife + kids; up to 1815 in Åkullsjön, Bygdeå; Nils dies 1809 and she becomes widow with 3 girls + 9 year old boy. Moves and then lives 1815-1817 in Kvarnrödjningen, where widow rem
2 CONC arried to Johan Nilsson of Åkullsjön.  Their only child was stillborn.
2 CONT Lisa lived 1834 to her death in 1841 in Sjöbäck at age 71 years, 6 mo., of alderdom (old age).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Sveriges Dödbok 9 1815-2022, ID SDB7_13496231.
2 CONT Kråken 14 person 193760, https://kråken.se/
